{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/908609-castlevania-mission","id":908609,"title":"Castlevania Mission","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-06T14:10:12-07:00","id":908609,"title":"Castlevania Mission","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> Have you thought about a mission with more action, in a distant castle, when the players enter in one of the rooms, skeletons rise from the ground and start attacks the players?<br /> Got it? Because I wish to do something similar about that.<br /> My question is mechanical. What kind of magic/effect that cause the creatures be summoned when the player enter in the room? What is skeleton in game system, some kind of Zombie?<br /> <br /> The idea is that the players enters in a Castle of a vampire Lord, boss of the campaign. Maybe the Castle is located in a Verge, and when the hunters players arrives, they face with a local totally different about hunting. Somewhere that the danger is in every room.<br /> Do you have any ideas to help with this scenario?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9723-winchester","name":"winchester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T14:36:10-07:00","id":908627,"title":"","content":"You could make it a zombie, basically taking a zombie write-up and maybe losing some Health and Strength. You don't need any particular mechanics to have a bunch of corpses or piles of bones rise up and become mobile. You would for their combat ability and survivability, however. Chronicles of Darkness has good advice for building Antagonists and Horrors. One of our posters wrote <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/599-zombie-creation-system-from-antagonists-updated-to-gmc\">this thread</a> for various zombies you might have. It's also in the Antagonists book.<br /> <br /> You're really going to want to find a way to let people heal. Otherwise people are going to have to rest for a few days after every room, which is okay because the creatures in the next room won't exist until they enter. Combat, alone, isn't an especially thrilling part of the Storyteller system, so you might want to add something more to it. Creatures that might be willing to side with players to attack the vampire lord or offer boons in exchange for loyalty or services.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T18:15:09-07:00","id":908770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/908609-castlevania-mission?p=908627#post908627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could make it a zombie, basically taking a zombie write-up and maybe losing some Health and Strength. You don't need any particular mechanics to have a bunch of corpses or piles of bones rise up and become mobile. You would for their combat ability and survivability, however. Chronicles of Darkness has good advice for building Antagonists and Horrors. One of our posters wrote <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/599-zombie-creation-system-from-antagonists-updated-to-gmc\">this thread</a> for various zombies you might have. It's also in the Antagonists book.<br /> <br /> You're really going to want to find a way to let people heal. Otherwise people are going to have to rest for a few days after every room, which is okay because the creatures in the next room won't exist until they enter. Combat, alone, isn't an especially thrilling part of the Storyteller system, so you might want to add something more to it. Creatures that might be willing to side with players to attack the vampire lord or offer boons in exchange for loyalty or services.</div> </div> </div> </div>My ideas: The Castle, exists in a Verge and it IS a Spirit (I could base this in some historical famous castle, some that resists too many invasions). So, the Spirit-Castle has a Comportamental Ban: it locks all exits until the a true warrior defeats every creatures in the room. So the doors open (like the games, that you cannot escape without defeat the creatures).<br /> <br /> About the cure, is a good idea a faster healing. Do you have any sugestion about it?<br /> But anyway, my players are templates, they have skills to heal faster than normal. I guess that it is not a great problem. Furthermore, I don't wish to create a entire mission inside the castle, like that fucking great amazing constructions in Castlevania. Just the ordinary size is enough. RPG inever was a good reference about simultaneity, compared with games, when you defeat dozens of enemies in seconds while you rolling the first dice in the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9723-winchester","name":"winchester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T21:33:47-07:00","id":908878,"title":"","content":"For most of the monsters, you should use the Brief Nightmares sub-system of Horror Creation.<br /> <br /> The appearance of the checkpoints is not as important as their availability. You should scale their rarity up and down to create more or less tension as you see fit. If the checkpoints are getting samey, consider placing additional risks + rewards.<br /> <br /> For example, there might be a ghost of a servant trapped inside a puzzle box, and they can only escape and talk clearly if freed. The ghost promises to reveal important information about the Castle and the Vampire Lord, and to help with spotting traps/treasures. The solutions to the puzzle are scattered...and certain monsters flock to the puzzle box to try and take it to parts unknown. Even free, the ghost cannot enter into every room, and they will move on to their next plane of existence before long.<br /> <br /> If your group doesn't like puzzles, focus on the mystery and rumors surrounding this Castle, and who the Vampire Lord is VS who he seems to be. Perhaps he has a Beast as a second in command with a hidden agenda. This Beast is the commander of other supernaturals, who may or may not be loyal. Either way, this Beast can use powers like Lair Tilts, Nightmares and Mother's Kiss remotely, but only around these gems carried by those under their command. You can try to kill each &quot;mini-boss&quot;, or reason and bargain to make them your allies...but they might insist on carrying the gems, or throw away a fake gems to create a false sense of security.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T05:52:33-07:00","id":911592,"title":"","content":"Something I've wanted to do lately is run an Innistrad/Bloodborne/Castlevania/Van Helsing inspired cheesy monster hunter game using Hunter and setting it in some vague fantasy historical location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}